<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2024/06/apple-tv-4k-new-orange.jpg" alt="" width="160" height="90" class="brief" align="left" style="float:left;margin:0 20px 20px 0;width:160px;height:auto;" />Apple's new Apple TV 4K will be powered by a standard A19 chip, up from the A15 in the current 2022 model, reports <em>Bloomberg</em>'s Mark Gurman. Writing in his <a href="https://www.bloomberg.com/news/newsletters/2026-10-11/apple-smart-home-launch-oct-13-plans-homeview-has-mid-november-release">Power On newsletter</a>, Gurman also said Apple has tested a refreshed Siri Remote with a speaker to make it easier to find between couch cushions. <br/>
<br/>
